{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/452337-exigents-martial-arts-and-sorcery","id":452337,"title":"Exigents, Martial Arts, and Sorcery","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-22T00:29:56-07:00","id":452337,"title":"Exigents, Martial Arts, and Sorcery","content":"We know that the build-your-own Exalted will have variable power levels, and some might even match the Celestial Exalted in puissance, so will they have access to the highest levels of martial arts or sorcery?<br /> <br /> Do you think Exigents should be able to summon Third Circle Demons? Master the March of Charcoal Spiders? Could there be pockets of civilization with working First Age wonders due to an Exigent maintaining them?<br /> <br /> This seems to break an fundamental assumption of the setting: that the returning Solars are bring back with them miracles and wonders that have been mostly absent since the Usurpation. At the same time, we know that there have been a handful of Solars popping up since then. Is &quot;for the last thousand years, a handful of Exigents have been able to do X&quot; change the setting any more than &quot;for the last thousand years, a handful of Solars have been able to do X?&quot;<br /> <br /> As good as the Wyld Hunt was under the Empress, I can't believe that not one Solar lived long enough to cast an Adamant Circle spell. Creation is a big place, so maybe the existence of a dozen Exigents who can reach these heights is fine. After all, while they might have Celestial/Solar/Sidereal tier abilities in <b>one area</b>, I doubt they'll have it in all of them.<br /> <br /> What do you think?<br /> <br /> What should the limits of Exigent charms/sorcery/MA/crafting be... if any?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 03-22-2015, 03:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T00:47:18-07:00","id":452366,"title":"","content":"Well, like you said, if a single Exigent is occasional able to make it, in a single avenue. to Solar tier power (or sidereal MA), then you've got a dangerous creature, but they'll likely only be able to reach such puissance within a single, defined avenue. Such as, for a bad example, an Exigent of the God of Widespread Ruin... they may be able to only cast Sorceries that cause widespread ruin.<br /> <br /> Such defined avenues I think are what restricts Exigents power. Whereas, the return of a Solar is that he's effectively a wild-card. They can do anything, you have no idea what a single one might do or what they've learned, and they're not shoehorned into any specific avenue...they can choose anything, at almost anytime, and excel.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T01:03:59-07:00","id":452375,"title":"","content":"I was under the impression that Exigents are pretty damn rare. Further each Exigent is totally different - they're more of a &quot;wild card&quot; Exalt in that any Exigent could possibly do anything. <br /> <br /> It's certainly possible that there are Exigents who are capable of casting Adamant Sorcery or using Sidereal Martial Arts, but they would probably be quite rare even among other Exigents.<br /> <br /> I think ultimately the best comparison for Exigents would be something like mutants in Marvel. Some mutants are incredibly powerful, others are really weak. Trying to classify what a Marvel Mutant should be able to do is kind of a lost cause because their power level and capabilities are so incredibly broad - for some their &quot;power&quot; is to have a third eye that doesn't work, while others have the power to completely reshape the universe. <br /> <br /> So I think, when the question comes up, &quot;Should Exigents be able to do X,&quot; the answer should be, &quot;Yes,&quot; but with the understanding that &quot;Exigent&quot; is sort of a catch-all term for ten million different potential types of Exalted, so while some could do X, many others might not be able to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T01:06:49-07:00","id":452377,"title":"","content":"I doubt there have actually been any Solar-tier, SCS-wielding Exigents in the years since the Usurpation. They are something that is notionally possible, but which are so rare as to be almost unheard of. Additionally, it's been implied that Exigents are connected directly to the UCS somehow, so I would not be surprised if they got a power-down when the UCS turned his face from Creation, which is only now being reversed with the Solars' return.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T01:20:43-07:00","id":452382,"title":"","content":"Like AnubisXY says, they're rare enough as it is, so it's unlikely there are any.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't say it does totally break the setting assumptions, even if there are.<br /> <br /> Also like you say, there have always been a handful of Solar Exalt turning up who can access Solar Circle Sorcery. And at least the Deathlords. Guys like Bagrash Kol who can do things hard even for a First Age Solar have periodically turned up, because Creation is a world that just rolls like that.<br /> <br /> Even if you don't have Exigents accessing the Solar tier powers, the fact that they can get Celestial power (in sorcery / charms) plus some things likely being easier for Exigents without Solar themes than Solars (because it fits more with their theme) means there will be new magic in the world never seen before even in the First Age.<br /> <br /> I'd also say the First Age was about having a complex society pushing forward on sorcerous projects with Solars leading from the front, and accumulating skill at the art of sorcery over a long time. So it's not like it really breaks the loss of the First Age very much.<br /> <br /> The thing is that there isn't the momentum when anything like that sporadically happens, in a way as if there were a whole host of people working towards this for a long time, with the backing of all the rest of the Exalted.<br /> <br /> The loss of First Age magi is an &quot;on the whole&quot; thing and one in a world where all the Exalted are underperforming their long term potential due to the Great Curse, policy, disaster, war, etc and where there have been multiple wholesale prehuman civilizations without any Exalted at all who on the whole probably had more magical prowess than the current Age of Sorrows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T01:26:10-07:00","id":452383,"title":"","content":"Both Samea and Arianna knows Solar Circle Sorcery from what I heard. They probably don't in Ex3 since &quot;The First Solar who Masters Adamant Circle Sorcery in the Age of Sorrow&quot; should be a title reserve only for the PC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T01:32:57-07:00","id":452386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/452337-exigents-martial-arts-and-sorcery?p=452377#post452377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I doubt there have actually been any Solar-tier, SCS-wielding Exigents in the years since the Usurpation. They are something that is notionally possible, but which are so rare as to be almost unheard of. Additionally, it's been implied that Exigents are connected directly to the UCS somehow, so I would not be surprised if they got a power-down when the UCS turned his face from Creation, which is only now being reversed with the Solars' return.</div> </div> </div> </div>In fact I believe it's been stated that in the absence of Solars and the attention of the Sun the flame of exigence has guttered in the past thousands of years. I think Ten Sheaves might even mention that it's the return of the Solars who allowed him to do what he did?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T01:58:56-07:00","id":452393,"title":"","content":"Re: Exigents, I wonder if they follow the same power vs Curse trade off as the other Exalted? So the more powerful among the Exigents also tend to be the more cursed, stymieing some of their ability to put their power into practice. I'm assuming they are cursed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T02:02:35-07:00","id":452394,"title":"","content":"From what I understand, there was a few Exigents, but not many. Recently there's been a big rise in the number of them.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I think that it perhaps could be conceptually possible, but only for really powerful ones within the particular limits.<br /> Like, perhaps the Exigent of Amoth City-Smiter could cast Rain of Doom, but only on cities.<br /> I don't really see much in the way of SMA being relevant, honestly, because they're just too esoteric.<br /> Like, you might say that the Exigent of the goddess of spiders should be able to use Charcoal March of Spiders, but actually that doesn't fit as well as straight spider powers.<br /> <br /> Thinking about it though, I wonder if this is looking at it the wrong way.<br /> Except for &quot;Exigent of the God of Martial Arts&quot; or &quot;Exigent of the God of Sorcery&quot; I think really martial arts and sorcery should be outside Exigent's themes.<br /> What I mean is, say you're an Exalt of the God of Drunkeness. You don't learn Drunken Master style, you have your own native charms powered by drunkenness. You learn Snake style in case you need to fight sober. You learn sorcery so you can turn your skin to bronze, conjure a cloud to carry you, summon and bind elementals to your will, and so on, because those are useful powers that you cannot learn as native charms because they're nothing to do with being drunk.<br /> Just like a Lunar or Abyssal might learn martial arts or sorcery to get things outside of their theme.<br /> <br /> So, except for the &quot;Exigent of the God of Martial Arts&quot; and the &quot;Exigent of the God of Sorcery&quot;, maybe Exigents should just be stuck with regular martial arts and terrestrial or celestial sorcery (depending on their power level). Because the point of these things is that they're not really related to your themes that much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T03:08:05-07:00","id":452450,"title":"","content":"I feel like the flexibility of the sorcerous project system means that, say you have an Exigent who it would be cool for them to have once performed magic beyond Celestial Circle Sorcery, they don't necessarily face the quandary of having to have Solar Circle Sorcery on tap just so that they can perform that singular miracle. Or likewise for an Exigent who is really well suited to the Terrestrial Circle Sorcery.<br /> <br /> So it would be a really extreme circumstance in which an Exigent really *needs* SCS as part of their character.<br /> <br /> Having a system of actions to support sorcerous projects / workings also allows some differentiation for Exalted in their sorcery beyond the simple hierarchy - maybe the Exigent of the Spider Goddess builds a sorcery through actions that are akin in some ways to a spider building a web or she can build webs (of a metaphorical sort) of connections and social influence which capture what she needs to fuel her sorcerous workings (without forcing the analogy too much)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T04:53:32-07:00","id":452524,"title":"","content":"I think one of the writers/devs said that people can generally cast workings higher than their level anyway, it's just harder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T06:15:36-07:00","id":452584,"title":"","content":"John said there are under 100 Exigents in existence as of RY 768 in one of the threads.<br /> <br /> I could see an Exigent hitting SMA but it'd have to be a very specific god to allow that and it's not like the Exigent would automatically have the institutional knowledge and training of the Sidereals or be likely to get it.<br /> <br /> SMA may not be its own specific Thing anymore though! TMA/CMA are not after all. It might just be a set of styles of which there is no record except in Heaven, and that jealously guarded by the Sidereals. I'd also bet that Sidereals have unique interactions with it and use it better than all other Exalts.<br /> <br /> SCS access - probably not but you also never know. Need a good reason, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T07:52:37-07:00","id":452686,"title":"","content":"Personally I would put them at the celestial level. So no solar sorcery or Sideral Martial arts, but stronger than the terrestrials in both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5257-queshire","name":"Queshire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T08:01:15-07:00","id":452689,"title":"","content":"I'd assume they have contextual access to things they shouldn't normally have full access to. The Chosen of Intoxicants would be able to learn SMAs based on drugs. The Chosen of a Road God would be able to tap into the higher circles of sorcery for the purpose of applying sorcerous working to roads. That sort of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}